Restore the original race finish WORD and lap-record DWORD layout.

Get_Race_Positions @443eb5 compares WORD [795c52] with 1. The overlapping
DWORD alias also reads car 1's WORD speed @795c54; a nonzero speed masks
car 0's completed laps and stops the normal finish counter from advancing.
Use only the original WORD. Preserve practice's separate finish policy,
refresh delays, destroyed-car checks and the existing rank sorting.

Calc_Track_Positions @443b3d multiplies level-1 by 12 and compares/stores
three DWORDs at 466e3c/40/44. The BYTE macros truncated fractional time and
made the C array's level stride 3 bytes instead of 12, corrupting neighboring
records. Restore all three signed DWORD aliases. This also restores the
original HUD and saved-record loading strides: FUN_0044d810 @44d81c uses
12-byte records and DWORD stores after loading unsigned saved WORDs.
Update_Jimmy_Spunk_Times @44d8ae..44d8c5 reads the same DWORD table, and its
later original WORD reads @44d96b/44d97c/44d992 retain their explicit casts.
The separate saved-record aliases and ordinary record-name UI still need
verification; this patch does not claim whole races, UI, or original A/V parity.

